+ * cpu_physical_memory_rw() call as the emulator's memory callback
+ * (whpx_emu_mmio_callback), so it reaches apic_mem_readl/writel with the same
+ * locking (prepare_mmio_access takes the BQL for the apic-msi region). Then
+ * RIP (and, for a load, the destination register) is written back with one
+ * WHvSetVirtualProcessorRegisters; a register store needs one
+ * WHvGetVirtualProcessorRegisters first. Returns false to use the stock path.
+ */
